cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite both the dataset and the paper it belongs to."
title: "Data release for: First Search for Ultraheavy Dark Matter Using a Magnetically Levitated Particle"
abstract: >-
  The complete limit-setting calculation behind the first ultraheavy dark matter
  search with a magnetically levitated particle, as two self-describing HDF5
  files, one per dark-matter-fraction and atmospheric-propagation hypothesis.
  Over a grid in sensor mode, per-neutron coupling, dark-matter mass and
  mediator range each stores the optimum-interval extremeness, the expected
  detected signal, and the expected number of in-reach transits, together with
  the measured per-mode detection efficiency curves, the impulse candidate lists
  and the live time. The halo is evaluated in the laboratory frame, at an Earth
  speed of 245 km/s recorded in the files' attributes. Exclusion at any
  confidence level is a level set of the
  stored extremeness, inside a mass window bounded by the kinematic wall and by
  the halo flux cut recorded in the files' attributes.
